cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "coxstream: Memory-Efficient Cox Proportional Hazards via Streaming Newton-Raphson"
abstract: >-
  An R implementation of the Cox proportional hazards model for datasets larger
  than RAM. It uses a single descending-order pass per Newton-Raphson iteration,
  so peak memory is O(p^2) regardless of the number of rows, and produces
  coefficients identical to survival::coxph() with the Efron tie correction.
type: software
